  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MORE MAMaZ: Scaling Up the Community Based Maternal and Newborn Health Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia has very high levels of maternal and new-born deaths. Many of these deaths could be prevented if women and new-borns got health care in good time. This application plans to extend a project called MaMaZ (Mobilising Access to Maternal Health Services in Zambia) that increased the numbers of women using maternal health services. They set up local solutions, such as transport systems, community savings schemes, and food banks, which help women to get care at the right time. Although it was successful, the programme only covered 25% of six districts. More MaMaZ will cover the rest of the communities in five of the districts. It will also learn which parts of the project are essential to achieve change and how they can be built in to government-funded district plans. The project will also introduce the approach in five new districts. As a result, more women will use life-saving maternal health services.</narrative>
  </description>
